[statement]
apk orders names byte by byte, and a byte above ASCII after every ASCII
byte: `x` comes before `é`, whose first byte is 0xc3. So `x` is decided
first and takes `p1`, and `é` then `p2`. Were 0xc3 a negative byte, `é`
would come first, take `p2`, and `p2` would answer `x` too. A name that is
not UTF-8 orders the same way: 0xff and 0x80 also come after `x`.

[repository]
P:p1
V:1
p:x
k:100

P:p2
V:1
p:x é=1
k:10

P:p3
V:1
p:é=1

[request]
é
x

[answer apk-tools 3.0.9-r0]
install p1 1
install p2 1
